<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE
        <ValidationRule> breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error. ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255
        characters, which is why the rationale is here.

        ADDED 2026-08-20 (Tranche 2, Workstream A4).
        🔴 THE SHARED RATIONALE FOR ALL FOUR A4 RULES ON THIS OBJECT LIVES IN
        Buyer_Counter_Price_Is_Positive.validationRule-meta.xml. READ IT THERE.

        🔴 ZERO IS PERMITTED AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE `&lt; 0` TEST. An all cash
        buyer closing immediately has a closing period of zero days. The requirements doc
        states this explicitly and it is the one thing about this rule that is easy to get
        wrong: `&lt;= 0` would refuse a real term.

        THE NOT(ISBLANK()) GUARD IS BELT AND BRACES HERE RATHER THAN LOAD BEARING, unlike on
        the two counter price rules where it separates "not countered" from "countered at
        zero". A blank Number in a validation rule comparison does not evaluate true against
        `&lt; 0` in any case. It is written anyway so all four rules on this object read the
        same way and so nobody has to re-derive the null semantics to review a one line
        change.
    -->
    <fullName>Closing_Period_Days_Not_Negative</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks a negative Closing Period Days on an offer. Zero is deliberately permitted: an all-cash buyer closing immediately is a real term. Blank is untouched. See Buyer_Counter_Price_Is_Positive for the shared A4 rationale on this object.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    NOT(ISBLANK(Closing_Period_Days__c)),
    Closing_Period_Days__c &lt; 0
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorMessage>Closing Period Days cannot be negative. Enter the number of days from execution to closing, or zero for an immediate close. Leave it blank if the buyer has not proposed a closing period.</errorMessage>
    <errorDisplayField>Closing_Period_Days__c</errorDisplayField>
</ValidationRule>
